From 32d0dc7c445aa12cc2cada6c4cc6e73b0bc768ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex automation <codex@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 11:43:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics_tcm_oncell: accept the KB2000 report layout

The panel controller on this device reports a 7-byte gesture prefix followed by
7 bytes per object, so 7, 14 and 21 byte reports are all legal. The driver
rejected the 14 and 21 byte forms as "invalid touch report length", which left
the touchscreen unusable even though the controller kept reporting. Account for
the prefix, validate against the real object stride, and keep the existing
framing and bounds checks.

Verified on hardware: with this layout the driver delivers ABS_MT_TRACKING_ID,
ABS_MT_POSITION_X/Y and BTN_TOUCH press/release for real finger input.
